    "description": "Collaborated with 2 classmates to develop a website using languages like JavaScript, HTML, CSS, Python, andMySQL that provided real time traffic data and allowed the users to report any incidents or accidents that occurred in the area.\nImplemented a user-registration feature using JavaScript andMySQL, enabling users to create their accounts.\nSet up a localMySQL server tomanage user accounts and reports, and ensure the server is configured to store and retrieve data efficiently. Additionally, configured access permissions to allow authorized users to interact with the database securely.\nImplemented real-time traffic data integration into system functionality by acquiring and configuring a GoogleMaps API key, enhancing user experience with accurate and up-to-date South Florida traffic information.\nSpearheaded the creation of a comprehensive Design Document to guide the structured and efficient development of our software system, aligning closely with stakeholders' vision outlined in the Software Requirements Document.\nComposed Test Cases to make sure that our softwaremet all the outlined requirements in the Software Requirements Document and to help identify any issues or bugs in the system in order to fix them.",
