    "description": "Developed a classic Snake game in Java using Object Oriented Programming to achieve the desired features.\nUtilized the JavaFX library for access to useful methods used to fully realize the GI and gamemechanics, including:\n- Snakemovement control: responsive user input handling for users to be able to control the snake’s directionmovement.\n- Food generation: random and dynamic placement of the food object (reward) on the board (game environment).\n- Collision detection: mechanism implemented to allow interactions between the snake, food, and itself (lose-condition).\n- Score and leveling system: score tracking system that increases the player’s level and game speed and difficulty, consequently.\nImplemented each feature by isolating them into classes utilizing OOP principles such as inheritance, polymorphism, and encapsulation in Java for modularity, scalability, andmaintainability, facilitating upcoming updates and debugging.",
